OL,3,GNEWSAChristmas tree to be lit for 80th
OL,4,Aconsecutive year
OL,5,
OL,6,FChristmas is a time for family and
OL,7,Ffriends to come together, but not many
OL,8,Fcan say they have stood in front of the
OL,9,Fexact same tree for generations.
OL,11,FThe lights of Grange-over-Sands' tree
OL,12,Fwill be switched on for the 80th
OL,13,Fconsecutive year on Saturday evening.
OL,15,FThe tree was planted in the 1860s when
OL,16,Fornamental gardens were created in the
OL,17,FCumbrian town, with funding from
OL,18,FFurness Railway. It was lit up for the
OL,19,Ffirst time in 1947, as communities were
OL,20,Frecovering from the impacts of World
OL,21,FWar Two.
OL,23,APub: 28-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NE Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
FL,397,390,260,160,0,100
